# EzFlutter V2 — Cursor Rules

You are working on EzFlutter V2, a production-ready Flutter boilerplate.

## Architecture
- lib/core/ = Framework layer (DO NOT modify unless asked)
- lib/core/ez/ = Ez* declarative page system
- lib/app/ = Application layer (this is where you work)

## Ez* System (ALWAYS prefer these over raw Flutter)
- List pages: extend `EzListPage<T>` (auto loading/error/empty/refresh)
- Detail pages: extend `EzDetailPage<T>` (renders from EzField definitions)
- Form pages: extend `EzFormPage` (auto field rendering + validation)
- Settings pages: extend `EzSettingsPage` (declarative sections)
- Fields: use `EzField.text()`, `.email()`, `.password()`, `.currency()`, `.select()`, `.toggle()`, `.date()`
- List items: use `EzTile(title:, subtitle:)`
- Services: extend `EzService`, use `guard()` instead of try/catch

## Patterns
- Models: @freezed + abstract class in lib/app/models/
- Services: @injectable + extends EzService in lib/app/services/
- Providers: @riverpod in lib/app/providers/
- Errors: Return Result<T>, never throw. Use guard() in EzService.

## After adding codegen files
Run: dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs

## CLI Tools
- `dart run tools/create_page.dart --name "X" --type list|form|settings|simple`
- `dart run tools/create_service.dart --name "X"`
